The real-time passages and the traffic messages come from the official API of
the Compagnie des Transports Strasbourgeois (CTS),
https://api.cts-strasbourg.eu/v1 (SIRI-lite), listed on transport.data.gouv.fr
("Réseau urbain CTS",
https://transport.data.gouv.fr/datasets/donnees-theoriques-gtfs-et-temps-reel-siri-lite-du-reseau-cts)
under the Licence Ouverte / Open Licence 2.0 of Etalab:
https://www.etalab.gouv.fr/licence-ouverte-open-licence/. Each user needs a
personal token of the open data portal of the CTS. The names and codes of the
stops and lines come from the open GTFS of the CTS,
https://opendata.cts-strasbourg.eu/google_transit.zip, under the same licence.
Source: CTS. The widgets show the source and the time of each reading.

The files under test/fixtures/gtfs are extracts of that GTFS (Licence Ouverte
2.0). The answers of the API used by the tests were built from its published
OpenAPI description (https://api.cts-strasbourg.eu/v1/swagger.json), not
recorded from it.

